{
 "format": "openchronology",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "George Washington, 1732–1799",
 "description": "A biography of George Washington on one line: his Virginia boyhood and surveying, the Virginia Regiment and the French and Indian War, Mount Vernon and the people enslaved there, the House of Burgesses, eight and a half years in command of the Continental Army, the Constitutional Convention, two terms as the first president, and his last years and will. A sample built from the cited sources, chiefly Wikipedia, the Papers of George Washington (Founders Online) and Mount Vernon’s research library.\n\n**How to read it.** Chapter headings mark the stages of his life. His life’s stages, homes, commands, offices, campaigns and family are durations; everything else is a moment with its sources. Related events (a battle and the one it led to) are linked. Colours follow the first tag: family, land, slavery, war, politics and the presidency, writing, and the wider world.\n\n**Dates.** Days in Virginia time, approximated as a fixed UTC−5. Britain and its colonies used the Julian calendar (Old Style) until September 1752; dates before then are converted to the Gregorian calendar, and the date as written at the time is kept as each moment’s original historical date. He was born on 11 February 1731/32, Old Style: 22 February 1732.",
 "presentation": {
  "mode": "gregorian",
  "unit": "",
  "scale": "1/1",
  "origin": "0/1",
  "version": 1,
  "offsetMinutes": -300,
  "significantDigits": 6
 },
 "tags": [
  "history",
  "biography",
  "united states",
  "george washington",
  "education"
 ],
 "plugins": [
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "rich-text-notes",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Rich text notes",
    "description": "Edit moment and stack notes visually, storing portable Markdown. Hover cards render safe headings, emphasis, lists, code and HTTPS links. HTML and images are not executed.",
    "fields": [],
    "notes": {
     "kind": "markdown"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-headings",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Headings",
    "description": "Let a moment act as a heading or marker: only its title shows, sized as a heading from level 1 to 6, and the title is what you click. Choose its font (Times New Roman by default). Headings still group into summaries with other moments.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "heading",
      "metadataKey": "headingLevel",
      "label": "Heading level"
     },
     {
      "kind": "font",
      "metadataKey": "headingFont",
      "label": "Heading font"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "heading",
     "metadataKey": "headingLevel"
    },
    "targets": [
     "moments"
    ]
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-colors",
    "version": 2,
    "name": "Moment colors",
    "description": "Choose muted semantic swatches or a custom color for moments and stack entries while preserving their white borders.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "metadataKey": "color",
      "label": "Moment color"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "color",
     "metadataKey": "color"
    },
